# SRG-APP-000915-AU-000400  -  CAT II
# The Central Log Server must provide protected storage for cryptographic
# keys with organization-defined safeguards and/or hardware protected key
# store.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations. Edit this
# file to change how this requirement is assessed here; it is read at run
# time. Regenerating overwrites it.

id:              SRG-APP-000915-AU-000400
group:           V-263583
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      derived
cci:             CCI-004910
control_rev5:    SC-28

contribution:    Splunk can hold its private keys in password-protected PEM files named
                 from configuration and stores those passwords in its own encrypted form
                 rather than in clear text, which is the key protection the product itself
                 can express.

governs:         inputs.conf - Configures inputs, distributed inputs such as forwarders, and file system
                 monitoring.
governs:         server.conf - Core server settings, including the certificates and protocols used to
                 protect management and replication traffic.

check:           inputs.conf [SSL] serverCert non_empty
check:           inputs.conf [SSL] sslPassword matches ^\$
check:           server.conf [sslConfig] serverCert not_equals $SPLUNK_HOME/etc/auth/server.pem
check:           server.conf [sslConfig] sslPassword matches ^\$
check:           server.conf [sslConfig] sslRootCAPath non_empty
# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
vendor:          server.conf [sslConfig] serverCert https://help.splunk.com/en/data-management/splunk-enterprise-admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/server.conf
vendor:          server.conf [sslConfig] sslPassword https://help.splunk.com/en/data-management/splunk-enterprise-admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/server.conf
vendor:          server.conf [sslConfig] sslRootCAPath https://help.splunk.com/en/data-management/splunk-enterprise-admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/server.conf
# --- end vendor verification

external:        Organization-defined safeguards for key storage, such as file system
                 permissions, disk encryption or a hardware protected key store, which the
                 check text leaves to the organization
external:        Any hardware security module or external key store, which this release's
                 configuration files do not reference
external:        The splunk.secret file and its operating system permissions, which protect
                 the encryption of the stored passwords
external:        Operating system ownership and permission bits on the certificate and
                 private key files

citation:        SRG-APP-000915-AU-000400 check text; SPLK-CL-000450 fix text;
                 inputs.conf.spec:990-1006; server.conf.spec:971-1009
finding:         Splunk's private key material is not protected to the extent the product
                 allows: a certificate password is stored in clear text or left at the
                 vendor default, or the instance still presents the certificate and key it
                 auto-generated on first start.
